<!-- The C.D. Cal. bankruptcy adversary complaint's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs)
     in the face of the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman: a typeface Central Guide 9004-1(b)(2)(C) lists) at
     12 pt (size 24 half points); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes (typst pitch, the numbered lines, Central Guide
     9004-1(b)(2)(F) double spacing) with a half-inch indent, and the headings in them; single lines in 12 pt boxes
     (typst pitch-single). Pleading paper as typst/cacb-adversary-complaint.typ: letter; top 1 in (line 1 at least
     1 inch down, Central Guide 9004-1(b)(2)(C)), 27 numbered lines of 24 pt (9004-1(b)(2)(B)(i) allows 28; the 28th would fall in the 1 in
     bottom margin the checks hold the text to), so the bottom margin is 1 in; left 1.5 in, right 1 in. The header (rIdHdrLines) holds the line numbers 1 to 27: a text box on
     the page, 1 in down, 1 in wide (the numbers end half an inch left of the text), right-aligned in exact 24 pt line
     boxes, on the baselines of the body lines. The pleading rules are page borders: a double rule at the text's left
     edge, a single rule at its right. The footer (rIdFooter1) is the typst one (Central Guide 9004-1(b)(2)(G)): the
     page number centered in a 12 pt line 6 pt below the last numbered line, then the paper's title (the SUBJECT
     property) and "ADV. NO." with the adversary number (COMMENTS) 4 pt below; docx/cacb-adversary.lua sets both
     properties from the sample. The footer's last line ends 38 pt above the page foot (760 twips). Twips: 20 x pt. -->
